---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[info] struct Subject { #[if_none] f: Option<T> }

---- yields ----
`#[if_none(...)]` requires an argument: `drop` or a string literal placeholder

---- input ----
#[derive(Enrichment)]
struct Subject { #[if_none] f: Option<T> }

---- yields ----
`#[if_none(...)]` requires an argument: `drop` or a string literal placeholder

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[info] struct Subject { #[if_none(bogus)] f: Option<T> }

---- yields ----
expected `drop` or a string literal placeholder, e.g. `#[if_none("n/a")]`

---- input ----
#[derive(Enrichment)]
struct Subject { #[if_none(bogus)] f: Option<T> }

---- yields ----
expected `drop` or a string literal placeholder, e.g. `#[if_none("n/a")]`

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[info] struct Subject { #[if_none(drop)] #[if_none(drop)] f: Option<T> }

---- yields ----
duplicate `#[if_none(...)]` attribute

---- input ----
#[derive(Enrichment)]
struct Subject { #[if_none(drop)] #[if_none(drop)] f: Option<T> }

---- yields ----
duplicate `#[if_none(...)]` attribute

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[info] struct Subject { #[if_none(drop)] f: T }

---- yields ----
`#[if_none(...)]` is only valid on `Option<T>` fields

---- input ----
#[derive(Enrichment)]
struct Subject { #[if_none(drop)] f: T }

---- yields ----
`#[if_none(...)]` is only valid on `Option<T>` fields
